    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0471" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/28351b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Foreign Trade Adviser of the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Rose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Commercial Adviser
                        of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crawford</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard</hi>: In order that there may
                    be no possible misunderstanding which might cause complications in the future,
                        <pb facs="0472" n="214" xml:id="pg214"/> in regard to the effect of the
                    negotiations and arrangements which are so pleasantly being conducted by us in
                    the matter of facilitating the shipment of goods to and from countries at war
                    with your Government and to neutral countries contiguous thereto, it seems
                    advisable that we should put on record our understanding that these negotiations
                    and arrangements are to be regarded as informal and unofficial and that neither
                    of our Governments is in any way committed thereby.</p>
                <p>Will you therefore be good enough to write me a letter confirming the above
                    statement of our understanding of the matter.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert F. Rose</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
